# Docker build context hygiene: the rmule-node image builds from the repo
# root, so keep multi-gigabyte and irrelevant trees out of the context upload.
#
# `target` is a bare pattern without `**/`, so it matches only a directory
# named that at the repo root by dockerignore's own rules
# (https://docs.docker.com/build/building/context/#dockerignore-files) — a
# leading slash is implied when there is no other slash in the pattern.
# `.scratch` is written `**/.scratch` instead, so it matches at any depth: the
# harness writes `.scratch/` and `target/bench-runs/` under the repo root
# today (`tools/interop-harness/src/cli/bench.rs`'s `DEFAULT_RUN_ROOT`,
# `rmule.rs`'s cargo caches), but a harness invocation from a different cwd
# (once, `tools/interop-harness/.scratch/interop-runs/*` rode into the
# context, breaking the `COPY` cache and forcing a full in-container compile
# every run) must not reopen this.
.git
**/.scratch
target
docs
**/*.pcap
